      },
      "worked": "Let the numbers be $x,y,z$. The possible triples fill the unit cube $0\\le x,y,z\\le1$, whose volume is 1.\n\nThe region $x+y+z<1$ is the tetrahedron with vertices $(0,0,0)$, $(1,0,0)$, $(0,1,0)$ and $(0,0,1)$, apart from its boundary. Its triangular base has area $\\frac12$ and its perpendicular height is 1.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}V&=\\frac13\\times\\frac12\\times1\\\\V&=\\frac16\\end{align*}$$\n\nUniform independent choices give probability proportional to volume, so\n$$\\Pr(x+y+z<1)=\\frac{\\frac16}{1}=\\frac16.$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
